1Password CLI</a></li><li><a href=3D"https://support.1password.com/develope=
r/#1password-developer-watchtower"><i class=3D"fa fa-chess-rook"></i>
1Password Developer Watchtower</a></li></ul></nav><br><h2 id=3D"turn-on-1pa=
ssword-developer"><img src=3D"https://i.1password.com/media/developer/icon-=
1password-developer.png" alt=3D"1Password Developer icon" width=3D"32" styl=
e=3D"vertical-align:-.3em"> Turn on 1Password Developer<a class=3D"anchorjs=
-link anchor" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" href=
=3D"https://support.1password.com/developer/#turn-on-1password-developer" s=
tyle=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h2><p>T=
o turn on the 1Password Developer setting in 1Password for Mac, Windows, or=
 Linux:</p><ol><li>Open and unlock the 1Password desktop app.</li><li>Selec=
t your account or collection at the top of the sidebar and choose <strong>S=
ettings</strong> &gt; <a href=3D"onepassword://settings/developers"><strong=
>Developer</strong></a>.</li><li>Turn on <strong>Show 1Password Developer e=
xperience</strong>.</li><li>To view activity logs with your SSH activity, m=
ake sure <strong>Record and display activity</strong> is also turned on.<p =
class=3D"note">This setting is turned on by default when you turn on 1Passw=
ord Developer in the sidebar.</p></li></ol><h2 id=3D"1password-ssh-agent"><=
img src=3D"https://i.1password.com/media/developer/icon-ssh-agent.png" alt=
=3D"1Password SSH icon" width=3D"32" style=3D"vertical-align:-.3em"> 1Passw=
ord SSH Agent<a class=3D"anchorjs-link anchor" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-a=
nchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" href=3D"https://support.1password.com/developer/=
#1password-ssh-agent" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: =
0.375em;"></a></h2><p>In the 1Password desktop app, select <strong>Develope=
r</strong> in the sidebar, then select <strong>View SSH agent</strong>.</p>=
<p>After you <a href=3D"https://developer.1password.com/docs/ssh/get-starte=
d">set up the 1Password SSH Agent</a>, you=E2=80=99ll be able to securely m=
anage your SSH keys, sign Git commits, and authorize all your SSH connectio=
ns with 1Password. You can then use the Developer section in the app to vie=
w and create private keys and review your recent SSH agent activity.</p><h3=
 id=3D"available-ssh-keys">Available SSH keys<a class=3D"anchorjs-link anch=
or" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" href=3D"https://=
support.1password.com/developer/#available-ssh-keys" style=3D"font: 1em / 1=
 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h3><p>This list shows SSH ke=
ys you=E2=80=99ve saved in 1Password that are <a href=3D"https://developer.=
1password.com/docs/ssh/agent/#eligible-keys">available to use with the SSH =
agent</a>.</p><div class=3D"row"><div class=3D"col-xs-12 col-sm-6"><ul><li>=
Select <strong>View details</strong> to open an SSH Key item in 1Password.<=
/li><li>Select <strong>Show all SSH keys</strong> to see a list of all the =
SSH keys you=E2=80=99ve saved in 1Password.</li><li>Select <strong>New SSH =
Key</strong> to <a href=3D"https://developer.1password.com/docs/ssh/manage-=
keys#generate-an-ssh-key">generate</a> a new SSH key or <a href=3D"https://=
developer.1password.com/docs/ssh/manage-keys#import-an-ssh-key">import</a> =
an existing key into 1Password.<p class=3D"note">Learn more about <a href=
=3D"https://developer.1password.com/docs/ssh/manage-keys#supported-ssh-key-=
types">supported key types</a>.</p></li></ul></div><div class=3D"col-xs-12 =
col-sm-6"><img class=3D"round border" style=3D"margin-top:1em" src=3D"https=
://i.1password.com/media/developer/available-ssh-keys.png" alt=3D"The SSH a=
gent screen showing a list of available SSH keys stored in 1Password" width=
=3D"100%"></div></div><p>If you use <a href=3D"https://support.1password.co=
m/multiple-accounts/">multiple accounts</a> in the 1Password app, you may s=
ee =E2=80=9CKey name unavailable=E2=80=9D for an SSH key saved in a locked =
account. To show the key name, select <strong>Unlock account</strong> or tu=
rn on <strong>Display key names when authorizing connections</strong> in th=
e <a href=3D"onepassword://settings/developers">Developer</a> settings.</p>=
<h3 id=3D"ssh-bookmarks">SSH Bookmarks<a class=3D"anchorjs-link anchor" ari=
a-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" href=3D"https://support=
.1password.com/developer/#ssh-bookmarks" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-ic=
ons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h3><p><a href=3D"https://developer.1pass=
word.com/docs/ssh/bookmarks">SSH Bookmarks</a> allow you to quickly connect=
 to the SSH hosts you frequently use, directly from 1Password.</p><div clas=
s=3D"row"><div class=3D"col-xs-12 col-sm-6"><ul><li>Select <strong>Bookmark=
</strong> from the Activity section to create a bookmark for an SSH host.</=
li><li>Select <strong>Connect</strong> in the Bookmark section to initiate =
and authorize a connection to an SSH host, without manually entering comman=
ds in the terminal.</li><li>Select the Actions menu for a bookmark to view =
the SSH Key item associated with a host or remove a bookmark.</li></ul></di=
v><div class=3D"col-xs-12 col-sm-6"><img class=3D"round border" style=3D"ma=
rgin-top:1em" src=3D"https://i.1password.com/media/developer/ssh-bookmarks.=
png" alt=3D"The SSH Bookmarks section showing bookmarked SSH hosts." width=
=3D"100%"></div></div><p>Learn more about <a href=3D"https://developer.1pas=
sword.com/docs/ssh/bookmarks">SSH Bookmarks</a>, including how to generate =
a <a href=3D"https://developer.1password.com/docs/ssh/bookmarks#ssh-configu=
ration-files">1Password configuration file</a> that automatically maps your=
 SSH hosts to keys.</p><p>If you=E2=80=99re an administrator, learn more ab=
out the <a href=3D"https://support.1password.com/team-policies/#sharing-and=
-permissions">app usage policy</a> for SSH Bookmarks.</p><h3 id=3D"ssh-acti=
vity-log">SSH activity log<a class=3D"anchorjs-link anchor" aria-label=3D"A=
nchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" href=3D"https://support.1password.c=
om/developer/#ssh-activity-log" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padd=
ing-left: 0.375em;"></a></h3><p>The activity log includes details about you=
r recent SSH activity, including:</p><div class=3D"row"><div class=3D"col-x=
s-12 col-sm-6"><ul><li>the application the SSH request originated from, the=
 SSH key that was used, and when the request was authorized</li><li>SSH req=
uests made from apps running in the background</li><li>SSH and Git commands=
 run in the terminal<br>(for example, <code>git pull</code> or <code>ssh ub=
untu@app-server</code>)</li></ul></div><div class=3D"col-xs-12 col-sm-6"><i=
mg class=3D"round border" style=3D"margin-top:1em" src=3D"https://i.1passwo=
rd.com/media/developer/ssh-activity-log-bookmark.png" alt=3D"The SSH activi=
ty log showing recent SSH authorization events, incluing an SSH host connec=
tion with a Bookmark button." width=3D"100%"></div></div><p>To clear the ac=
tivity log, select <strong>Clear activity</strong>.</p><p>Learn more about =
<a href=3D"https://support.1password.com/developer/#data-retention-and-priv=
acy">data retention and privacy</a> with 1Password Developer.</p><div class=
=3D"more box icon-box"><h4 class=3D"box-header" id=3D"read-more">Read More<=
a class=3D"anchorjs-link anchor" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=
=3D"=EE=A7=8B" href=3D"https://support.1password.com/developer/#read-more" =
style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h4><p>=
</p><ul><li><a href=3D"https://developer.1password.com/docs/ssh/get-started=
">Get started with 1Password for SSH</a></li><li><a href=3D"https://develop=
er.1password.com/docs/ssh/git-commit-signing">Sign Git commits with SSH</a>=
</li><li><a href=3D"https://developer.1password.com/docs/ssh/bookmarks">Use=
 SSH Bookmarks</a></li><li><a href=3D"https://developer.1password.com/docs/=
ssh/agent/forwarding">Use SSH agent forwarding with 1Password</a></li></ul>=
<p></p></div><h2 id=3D"1password-environments"><img src=3D"https://i.1passw=
ord.com/media/icon-environments.png" alt=3D"1Password Environments icon" wi=
dth=3D"32" style=3D"vertical-align:-.2em"> 1Password Environments<a class=
=3D"anchorjs-link anchor" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=
=A7=8B" href=3D"https://support.1password.com/developer/#1password-environm=
ents" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></=
h2><p>In the 1Password desktop app, select <strong>Developer</strong> in th=
e sidebar, then select <strong>Environments</strong>.</p><p>After you set u=
p <a href=3D"https://developer.1password.com/docs/environments">1Password E=
nvironments</a>, you can use environments to simplify management of environ=
ment variables and secrets within 1Password and share access with other tea=
m members. You can also use the <a href=3D"https://developer.1password.com/=
docs/environments/aws-secrets-manager/">1Password AWS Secrets Manager integ=
ration</a> with Environments to securely sync secrets to AWS Secrets Manage=
r.</p><h2 id=3D"1password-cli"><img src=3D"https://i.1password.com/media/de=
veloper/icon-cli.png" alt=3D"1Password CLI icon" width=3D"32" style=3D"vert=
ical-align:-.2em"> 1Password CLI<a class=3D"anchorjs-link anchor" aria-labe=
l=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" href=3D"https://support.1pass=
word.com/developer/#1password-cli" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; p=
adding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h2><p>In the 1Password desktop app, select <st=
rong>Developer</strong> in the sidebar, then select <strong>View CLI</stron=
g>.</p><p>To install 1Password CLI, select <strong>View installation instru=
ctions</strong> and follow the steps for your operating system.</p><p>You c=
an also <a href=3D"https://developer.1password.com/docs/cli/app-integration=
">use the app to sign in to 1Password in the terminal</a>. From the CLI pag=
e, select <strong>Settings</strong> and turn on <strong>Integrate with 1Pas=
sword CLI</strong>.</p><p>After you set up 1Password CLI, you=E2=80=99ll be=
 able to use 1Password to:</p><ul><li>Provision secrets, automate administr=
ative tasks, and more from the command line</li><li>Review your recent <a h=
ref=3D"https://support.1password.com/developer/#1password-cli-activity-log"=
>1Password CLI activity</a>.</li></ul><p>In the 1Password desktop app, sele=
ct the Developer category in the sidebar, then select <strong>View CLI</str=
ong>.</p><h3 id=3D"1password-cli-activity-log">1Password CLI activity log<a=
 class=3D"anchorjs-link anchor" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D=
"=EE=A7=8B" href=3D"https://support.1password.com/developer/#1password-cli-=
activity-log" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;=
"></a></h3><p>The activity log includes details about recent 1Password CLI =
activity, including:</p><div class=3D"row"><div class=3D"col-xs-12 col-sm-7=
"><ul><li>the application where the 1Password CLI command was run</li><li>t=
he name of the account that was accessed</li><li>when the request was made<=
/li><li>the <code>op</code> command that was run from the terminal (for exa=
mple, <code>op group user list</code> or <code>op run --env-file=3D.env -- =
./my-app</code>)</li></ul></div><div class=3D"col-xs-12 col-sm-5"><img clas=
s=3D"round border" style=3D"margin-top:1em" src=3D"https://i.1password.com/=
media/developer/cli-activity-log.png" alt=3D"The 1Password CLI screen showi=
ng a list of recent activity from terminal applications where `op` commands=
 were run." width=3D"100%"></div></div><p>To clear the activity log, select=
 <strong>Clear activity</strong>.</p><p>Learn more about <a href=3D"https:/=
/support.1password.com/developer/#data-retention-and-privacy">data retentio=
n and privacy</a> with 1Password Developer.</p><div class=3D"more box icon-=
box"><h4 class=3D"box-header" id=3D"read-more-1">Read More<a class=3D"ancho=
