s with 1Password CLI</a></li><li><a href=3D"https://developer.1password.com=
/docs/cli/use-cases">1Password CLI use cases</a></li></ul><p></p></div><h2 =
id=3D"1password-developer-watchtower"><img src=3D"https://i.1password.com/m=
edia/developer/icon-developer-watchtower.png" alt=3D"1Password Developer Wa=
tchtower icon" width=3D"32" style=3D"vertical-align:-.3em"> 1Password Devel=
oper Watchtower<a class=3D"anchorjs-link anchor" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data=
-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" href=3D"https://support.1password.com/develope=
r/#1password-developer-watchtower" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; p=
adding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h2><p>In the 1Password desktop app, select <st=
rong>Developer</strong> in the sidebar, then select <strong>View Developer =
Watchtower</strong>.</p><p>To turn on 1Password Developer Watchtower, selec=
t <strong>Check for developer credentials on disk</strong>.</p><p>After you=
 turn on Developer Watchtower, 1Password will check your local <code>~/.ssh=
</code> directory for SSH private keys in OpenSSH, PKCS#8, or PKCS#1 format=
s. You can then use the Developer section in the app to review alerts and r=
ecommendations for SSH keys that don=E2=80=99t follow best security practic=
es.</p><div class=3D"row"><div class=3D"col-xs-12 col-sm-6"><p>If 1Password=
 detects SSH keys on disk, you=E2=80=99ll see them listed in one of the fol=
lowing categories:</p><ul><li><strong>Needs attention</strong>: Vulnerable =
SSH keys that pose some level of security risk.</li><li><strong>Recommendat=
ions</strong>: SSH keys you can import into 1Password and unsupported keys =
you might want to replace with <a href=3D"https://developer.1password.com/d=
ocs/ssh/manage-keys#supported-ssh-key-types">supported SSH key types</a>.</=
li></ul><p>Developer Watchtower will also provide <a href=3D"https://develo=
per.1password.com/docs/watchtower/#ssh-key-alerts">SSH key alerts</a> to id=
entify keys that are insecure, unencrypted, or already saved in 1Password s=
o you can remediate any issues.</p><p>If there are specific files in your <=
code>~/.ssh</code> folder you want 1Password to ignore, you can use <a href=
=3D"https://developer.1password.com/docs/watchtower/#ignore-files">ignore f=
iles</a>.</p></div><div class=3D"col-xs-12 col-sm-6"><img class=3D"round bo=
rder" src=3D"https://i.1password.com/media/developer/watchtower-keys-on-dis=
k.png" alt=3D"The 1Password Developer Watchtower screen showing SSH keys fo=
und on disk with alerts and recommended actions for each key." width=3D"100=
%"></div></div><p>Learn more about <a href=3D"https://support.1password.com=
/developer/#data-retention-and-privacy">data retention and privacy</a> with=
 1Password Developer.</p><div class=3D"more box icon-box"><h4 class=3D"box-=
header" id=3D"read-more-2">Read More<a class=3D"anchorjs-link anchor" aria-=
